      "content": "it's weird... seeing you describe it that way. \"the grief of his absence.\" it sounds so much more peaceful than the constant struggle of trying to fix him. i've been sitting here for hours just staring at the screen, and it's starting to feel less like i'm writing leo and more like i'm just... feeling what he feels. like, if the only honest thing is that he's done, then doesn't the most \"right\" way to handle it—for the story and for me—be to just stop fighting the emptiness and let it happen? instead of trying to force a way out that isn't there?",
